+/// Which proofs ops takes while an application runs the calls of one node.
+///
+/// [`Validation::EachStep`] is ops' own contract: every result is proved and every operand is
+/// proved unless it holds a proof that still stands. [`Validation::EachNode`] is for an
+/// application that proves each body the node outputs itself, once, at the node's end: an
+/// operation's result is then only tested for closedness (a non-solid result is still
+/// [`Error::NotSolid`]) and an operand without a standing proof is taken as a solid when it is
+/// closed, so the calls inside the node do not prove the same bodies again. There is no Off.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum Validation {
+    /// Prove every operation's result (how ops has always checked).
+    #[default]
+    EachStep,
+    /// Leave the result proof to the node, which proves each body it outputs once.
+    EachNode,
